msgctxt "doc/texinfo/api.texi|Namespace gmsh/model|paragraph|gmsh/model/getClosestPoint"
msgid "Get the points @code{closestCoord} on the entity of dimension @code{dim} (1 or 2) and tag @code{tag} to the points @code{coord}, by orthogonal projection. @code{coord} and @code{closestCoord} are given as x, y, z coordinates, concatenated: [p1x, p1y, p1z, p2x, ...]. @code{parametricCoord} returns the parametric coordinates t on the curve (if @code{dim} == 1) or u and v coordinates concatenated on the surface (if @code{dim} = 2), i.e. [p1t, p2t, ...] or [p1u, p1v, p2u, ...]. The closest points can lie outside the (trimmed) entities: use @code{isInside()} to check."
msgstr ""

