#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Surfaces|paragraph|Plane Surface ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @};"
msgid "Create a plane surface. The @var{expression} inside the parentheses is\nthe plane surface's tag; the @var{expression-list} on the right hand\nside should contain the tags of all the curve loops defining the\nsurface. The first curve loop defines the exterior boundary of the\nsurface; all other curve loops define holes in the surface.  A curve loop\ndefining a hole should not have any curves in common with the exterior\ncurve loop (in which case it is not a hole, and the two surfaces should\nbe defined separately). Likewise, a curve loop defining a hole should not\nhave any curves in common with another curve loop defining a hole in the\nsame surface (in which case the two curve loops should be combined)."
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 585fadfd2917c0731fba949ba7eea6c5d4c461b1741e81d300efd988a2785430
#. source_hash: 80fc76cc9bbe82a370b68cef155a360b3685da67e0ebb56680a739472601adc9
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Surfaces|item|Surface ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @} < In Sphere @{ @var{expression} @}, Using Point @{ @var{expression-list} @} >;"
msgid "Surface ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @} < In Sphere @{ @var{expression} @}, Using Point @{ @var{expression-list} @} >;"
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 5e91f089f4334684dd0bee2131f2d9effdd2e31fc8f75f7fba7a2915aeddb6ba
#. source_hash: a268602a3d85b6268829c17bd1842b6a2097e87e751ccf381b5b265187785164
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Surfaces|paragraph|Surface ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @} < In Sphere @{ @var{expression} @}, Using Point @{ @var{expression-list} @} >;"
msgid "Create a surface filling. With the built-in kernel, the first curve\nloop should be composed of either three or four curves, the surface is\nconstructed using transfinite interpolation, and the optional @code{In\nSphere} argument forces the surface to be a spherical patch (the extra\nparameter gives the tag of the center of the sphere). With the\nOpenCASCADE kernel, a BSpline surface is constructucted by optimization\nto match the bounding curves, as well as the (optional) points provided\nafter @code{Using Point}."
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 14c4d27a72d97536c042e575b3e3c4fa874bf8763a5b81874a3583c8107fc03c
#. source_hash: dbbaf11b7aab901e5c3fde75010bf6b35f22bcd8ea450d2c0fb54eb80fbf548c
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Surfaces|item|BSpline Surface ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @};"
msgid "BSpline Surface ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @};"
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: d2706c68f633ea59f9e5db55a64b9b5963c711d30ad1d9b7a3aad97ed48cfd49
#. source_hash: c5134354fa3bbaf6e11f3f20776e38e4a47f3baf75e3cdb34c9826d0f13c31fc
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Surfaces|paragraph|BSpline Surface ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @};"
msgid "Create a BSpline surface filling. Only a single curve loop made of 2, 3\nor 4 BSpline curves can be provided. @code{BSpline Surface} is only\navailable with the OpenCASCADE kernel."
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 114d5d71296c6ad89cf0248e38989b230549aaedfb3fa6f39fb6f09d7cef7759
#. source_hash: 0ad5885398c0a785d74dde0c6ae1361593bdc66fc719801d44db7376b30d7687
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Surfaces|item|Bezier Surface ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @};"
msgid "Bezier Surface ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @};"
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: afee9a92fab01aa503a7fd1f286ab7ea34a70ab74c870a75fc4e5da0ca4dee7c
#. source_hash: f7ed0793127574c518a58e3e721a22ec2e846ae2c19da1c291efc2141efd8c3e
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Surfaces|paragraph|Bezier Surface ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @};"
msgid "Create a Bezier surface filling. Only a single curve loop made of 2, 3\nor 4 Bezier curves can be provided. @code{Bezier Surface} is only\navailable with the OpenCASCADE kernel."
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 4f6e4e8d23376c4694a6701d50a96a72b12cb1ef532e670e9ed3d4fc1cb6774f
#. source_hash: 04481b3ae1a3105959ee5a492695a1df08dabe208d637d11e0aff1a19cf94696
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Surfaces|item|Disk ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @};"
msgid "Disk ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @};"
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 415697f73169677c09ddaea4195fff016bcf4c2a1ab64ae9970efafb1625f2fe
#. source_hash: 25b24afab38b4b640abf3e4ac92a710b48e8c5b22b3031411b863b11469dd6c9
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Surfaces|paragraph|Disk ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @};"
msgid "Creates a disk. When four expressions are provided on the right hand\nside (3 coordinates of the center and the radius), the disk is circular.\nA fifth expression defines the radius along Y, leading to an ellipse.\n@code{Disk} is only available with the OpenCASCADE kernel."
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 55002dbb60d734370e277d9aebc6a41c8182fbef798f01a10a6daf4d7b1186b5
#. source_hash: 9eaeff798f0f08b0f2177025434e0343396ffea3701efac3019ac6a1e262e9e0
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Surfaces|item|Rectangle ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @};"
msgid "Rectangle ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @};"
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 0b4735aa3bbb9cd95b36c1b812eeed7242fee5be7f55941b86ac4a2899389b99
#. source_hash: 9a35a05a6ed76d249bc7f2a85aeb9b952c18fd5f5feb8561b46aa2314087877e
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Surfaces|paragraph|Rectangle ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @};"
msgid "Create a rectangle. The 3 first expressions define the lower-left\ncorner; the next 2 define the width and height. If a 6th expression is\nprovided, it defines a radius to round the rectangle\ncorners. @code{Rectangle} is only available with the OpenCASCADE kernel."
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: a9040fe58df0194d2f37d958715d78012cab937b26ba546d1b45c77a9c4a21ec
#. source_hash: 8ecbdfcbd46fdcdc09845316daac24a15907b144cc2b130fcda6b38abdae6097
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Surfaces|item|Surface Loop ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @} < Using Sewing >;"
msgid "Surface Loop ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @} < Using Sewing >;"
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 31ba7fad432c275dbeebb242b05904c698f68d169f27a5b7a1cc4fbabc998f05
#. source_hash: 6d4f298e02d9a4317bb7e70bd59e258fe6a96147390bb85c0a895300308c13d1
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Surfaces|paragraph|Surface Loop ( @var{expression} ) = @{ @var{expression-list} @} < Using Sewing >;"
msgid "Create a surface loop (a shell). The @var{expression} inside the\nparentheses is the surface loop's tag; the @var{expression-list} on the\nright hand side should contain the tags of all the surfaces that\nconstitute the surface loop. A surface loop must always represent a\nclosed shell, and the surfaces should be oriented consistently (using\nnegative tags to specify reverse orientation). (Surface loops are used\nto create volumes: see @ref{Volumes}.) With the OpenCASCADE kernel, the\noptional @code{Using Sewing} argument allows to build a shell made of\nsurfaces that share geometrically identical (but topologically\ndifferent) curves."
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 98522792c6810fe66b6d528a3f5d68e7bd3cce86560f9d3599295ac06d14621d
#. source_hash: 561bd9bb1d00df48a53daeb0f4aba8086d28f0b9b7bb03da75211d5f01b4e974
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Surfaces|item|Physical Surface ( @var{expression} | @var{string-expression} <, @var{expression}> ) <+|->= @{ @var{expression-list} @};"
msgid "Physical Surface ( @var{expression} | @var{string-expression} <, @var{expression}> ) <+|->= @{ @var{expression-list} @};"
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 78fbd6eb7d20a76c529c656e3d4191641f2504064c2f4b0f9144034c7608a87a
#. source_hash: 49ccd6d82f7b62316a6b91a90346dbb03e4e1798a6d5084353e010e710d1b4ee
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Surfaces|paragraph|Physical Surface ( @var{expression} | @var{string-expression} <, @var{expression}> ) <+|->= @{ @var{expression-list} @};"
msgid "Create a physical surface. The @var{expression} inside the parentheses\nis the physical surface's tag; the @var{expression-list} on the right\nhand side should contain the tags of all the elementary surfaces that\nneed to be grouped inside the physical surface.  If a\n@var{string-expression} is given instead instead of @var{expression}\ninside the parentheses, a string label is associated with the physical\ntag, which can be either provided explicitly (after the comma) or not\n(in which case a unique tag is automatically created).  In some mesh\nfile formats (e.g. MSH2), specifying negative tags in the\n@var{expression-list} will reverse the orientation of the mesh elements\nbelonging to the corresponding elementary surfaces in the saved mesh\nfile."
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 17f4936c265aceb21d32b6a2ef8c71a293a368477e83dca0af338320b5232c0d
#. source_hash: d6113f9ed6fb059ae5e15d431dee1ddefd841de45d402811596ab1ef8e043d58
