#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Post-processing scripting commands|paragraph|340777e31ba84dcf9b178a6a7f56a7369ccd5343ea973f4ffc48f6a905e7c3ec"
msgid "The ordering of the nodes is given in @ref{Node ordering}."
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 6b2c10cbca28fb68cbfae5e949e3551b270545337e894f8ccf1df0982da62c37
#. source_hash: 8d1ee6480c825a18b608b9104fff25885bf6ae89ab5ce810ecd44da65135a458
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Post-processing scripting commands|paragraph|0f247df3f9ea32cc7f40b59216ee5e6c6fe5be44783651394622e8c99dfadb52"
msgid "The values are given by time step, by node and by component, i.e.:"
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 04892ccad1219b1bfd3a1a7d309988b1dc83e17f1c92e1bf944d314737f5afe1
#. source_hash: d43e7ee20bea840c2e0515ac78f64b591b623005f22d96e111f0b33164f6a899
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Post-processing scripting commands|paragraph|0b47e7b680c511fcb0c18f0a759fa99dc90d3c08ed28755b6de1f37a88ef06ef"
msgid "For the 2D text objects, the two first @w{@var{expression}s} in\n@var{coordinates} give the X-Y position of the string in screen\ncoordinates, measured from the top-left corner of the window. If the first\n(respectively second) @var{expression} is negative, the position is measured\nfrom the right (respectively bottom) edge of the window. If the value of the\nfirst (respectively second) @var{expression} is larger than 99999, the\nstring is centered horizontally (respectively vertically). If the third\n@var{expression} is equal to zero, the text is aligned bottom-left and\ndisplayed using the default font and size. Otherwise, the third\n@var{expression} is converted into an integer whose eight lower bits give\nthe font size, whose eight next bits select the font (the index corresponds\nto the position in the font menu in the GUI), and whose eight next bits\ndefine the text alignment (0=bottom-left, 1=bottom-center, 2=bottom-right,\n3=top-left, 4=top-center, 5=top-right, 6=center-left, 7=center-center,\n8=center-right)."
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: d0081f25fb0620bcf9910bde43ca0285fa5c9537ccf7146d6572d5f0c24c68f5
#. source_hash: c127f77f677a4a4e613ee154190e3c490d2d0074221855e864e507099a112240
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Post-processing scripting commands|paragraph|c2685e999e13032eda9673672cd6208be62a0723739de62bdbfefa26d9f707ed"
msgid "For the 3D text objects, the three first @w{@var{expression}s} in\n@var{coordinates} give the XYZ position of the string in model (real\nworld) coordinates.  The fourth @var{expression} has the same meaning as the\nthird @var{expression} in 2D text objects."
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 9f9f0332c0ed43d1c135dc35af1245a23f38536d699cb57481aee1335e394319
#. source_hash: 2eb88eb61e485b38297d8c80665924de09fc0baacb733b8b5ac5b9b973e29c86
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Post-processing scripting commands|paragraph|590ef04a0aa23b361578bc327e52c8ef6ffa96d3e142853068ecc7e77249df12"
msgid "For both 2D and 3D text objects, the @var{values} can contain an\narbitrary number of @w{@var{string-expression}s}. If the\n@var{string-expression} starts with @code{file://}, the remainder of the\nstring is interpreted as the name of an image file, and the image is\ndisplayed instead of the string. A format string in the form\n@code{@@wxh} or @code{@@wxh,wx,wy,wz,hx,hy,hz}, where @code{w} and\n@code{h} are the width and height (in model coordinates for @code{T3} or\nin pixels for @code{T2}) of the image, @code{wx,wy,wz} is the direction\nof the bottom edge of the image and @code{hx,hy,hz} is the direction of\nthe left edge of the image."
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 78b524f3d34b6d6e0488956a4e6eed3e25bef648d8c316bc0046ea2a9020e35d
#. source_hash: 0f9cd829736b5f4381cdaf794cf49d9f1444d5a71247370f49823c6bd837b5c2
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Post-processing scripting commands|paragraph|c1831a3a6be76c845bc4dde52deff00a93c788fcc627f6651a5b0f2a835b1b8d"
msgid "The optional @code{TIME} list can contain a list of expressions giving the\nvalue of the time (or any other variable) for which an evolution was saved."
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 15200aa3a0285777304651f43ff1605efe6b59206205cc6ad6b8236455da5eeb
#. source_hash: d8339a633d0fd12f826a3f60cfd9ed3bebb2ec5bc63b0a5a04c9e801af1004dd
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Post-processing scripting commands|paragraph|a5c2d056196a03c5307b379e8a324dfe5aae0e0932e3393266a6b9cfb7caba77"
msgid "The optional @code{INTERPOLATION_SCHEME} lists can contain the\ninterpolation matrices used for high-order adaptive visualization."
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 4eb4ca2acd4515607f58aba61b41436391d541d61bddd30c1d614211409e435f
#. source_hash: b945998a168cfdfd3b04662d575c92dd370ed902c7032048fc7e072123a84984
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Post-processing scripting commands|paragraph|265fe4dbef5375477bfc2a6da4295fd232ce4c59b24fa444e23d6c968dec5eb2"
msgid "Let us assume that the approximation of the view's value over an element\nis written as a linear combination of @var{d} basis functions\n@var{f}[@var{i}], @var{i}=0, ..., @var{d}-1 (the coefficients being\nstored in @var{values}). Defining @var{f}[@var{i}] = Sum(@var{j}=0, ...,\n@var{d}-1) @var{F}[@var{i}][@var{j}] @var{p}[@var{j}], with\n@var{p}[@var{j}] = @var{u}^@var{P}[@var{j}][0]\n@var{v}^@var{P}[@var{j}][1] @var{w}^@var{P}[@var{j}][2] (@var{u},\n@var{v} and @var{w} being the coordinates in the element's parameter\nspace), then @var{val-coef-matrix} denotes the @var{d} x @var{d} matrix\n@var{F} and @var{val-exp-matrix} denotes the @var{d} x @var{3} matrix\n@var{P}."
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 358e1aa7f8d98437c51fb51ad944a05e46f2c9b73178c95e6975c14dd4930179
#. source_hash: ac01904ec9759dd4db4a0107752cbe420df6a19daf49c8de9affe9ca9cfd9efc
#: doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi
msgctxt "doc/texinfo/gmsh.texi|Post-processing scripting commands|paragraph|8116c45a9d7de6aa9ba96bf0893f3eec5800eb56b877192f5e572b0840457773"
msgid "In the same way, let us also assume that the coordinates @var{x},\n@var{y} and @var{z} of the element are obtained through a geometrical\nmapping from parameter space as a linear combination of @var{m} basis\nfunctions @var{g}[@var{i}], @var{i}=0, ..., @var{m}-1 (the coefficients\nbeing stored in @var{coordinates}). Defining @var{g}[@var{i}] =\nSum(@var{j}=0, ..., @var{m}-1) @var{G}[@var{i}][@var{j}]\n@var{q}[@var{j}], with @var{q}[@var{j}] = @var{u}^@var{Q}[@var{j}][0]\n@var{v}^@var{Q}[@var{j}][1] @var{w}^@var{Q}[@var{j}][2], then\n@var{geo-coef-matrix} denotes the @var{m} x @var{m} matrix @var{G} and\n@var{geo-exp-matrix} denotes the @var{m} x @var{3} matrix @var{Q}."
msgstr ""

#. unit_id: 556f547f6cf06a19459fd3428bb5cf7518b49fdbb792706c5a7484a56338eb3e
